window.products.push({"id":444199,"name":"The Butterflies of the World Educational Science Classroom Chart Print Poster 24x36","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":10.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61gRHUpoT9L._AC_.jpg","description":"The Lepidoptera order / clade contains the butterflies and moths. There are over 180,000 known species. In general, butterflies fly during the day and moths fly at night. The most obvious physical difference between them is the feelers, or antennae. Most butterflies have slender filamentous ones that are club-shaped at the end. Moths, on the other hand, often have comb-like or feathery antennae, or ones that are filamentous and unclubbed. This popular poster shows over 100 of the most colorful butterflies, as well as a few moths. The captions cite common name, biological name, and where they are found. These beautiful insects are grouped by continent or other geographic area. Unique globe and arrow icons identify the location","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61gRHUpoT9L._AC_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Picture Peddler","source_asin":"B01HSWMY3I","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-444199","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01HSWMY3I","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B01HSWMY3I","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
